#undef NDEBUG
// Review HA: Declare and Heuristics++ keyed by typed XES columns on an XES
// upload's DataFrame and LazyFrame shapes.
//
// - pandas Declare keyed by a column of ints (past int64 too), floats,
//   booleans, dates or a mix: the model pm4py answers through its rules
//   frame (rule keys str() of the MultiIndex's objects, one-element keys
//   where the second activity is missing or falsy, ints of a level with gaps
//   read back as floats, each NaN of a float64 column its own activity, NaN
//   and NaT unequal to themselves), and its KeyError and TypeError (whose
//   operands follow the hash seed: those cases compare the error class).
// - Heuristics++ keyed by such a column: one node per Python-equal object
//   (a float64 column's ints past int64 as floats, each NaN its own node),
//   the TypeErrors of its concurrency keys and dependency pairs, NaN pairs
//   keyed as Python's sorted() leaves them, and start_timestamp as the
//   activity key read as the interval's start too.
//
// Expected values are pm4py 2.7.22 black-box on the same inputs
// (review-harness round-ha: tc/mkha.py, ct/u64.py).
//
// Usage: minera_server_review_ha_tests <minera_server>

